          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Personal Life</strong><br>\nMárquez married Mercedes Barcha in 1958, with whom he had two sons, Rodrigo and Gonzalo. His marriage lasted until his death and was a significant part of his life and writing. Márquez lived in Mexico for many years and had a close circle of friends, including Fidel Castro.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Political Views and Influence</strong><br>\nMárquez's political views were shaped by his experiences in Colombia and his criticism of imperialism and violence. He was an ardent supporter of leftist causes and was friends with several Latin American leaders. His fame as a writer brought international attention to political and social issues in Latin America.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy and Death</strong><br>\nGabriel García Márquez passed away on April 17, 2014, at the age of 87. His death marked the loss of a literary giant whose works have influenced not only literature but also the understanding of Latin American culture and politics. His legacy continues to inspire readers and writers around the world.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
